From: Duron27 <duron27@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] client-package: zip the OpenMW programs of a build, with the multiplayer mod built in, to share

cmake --build . --target client-package makes two zips in the build folder:
- openmw-multiplayer-client-<system>-<cpu>-portable.zip: every program that was built (game, launcher, wizard, OpenMW-CS, the
  tools), their resources with the multiplayer scripts added to the built-in lists, the config files, the libraries they need
  (found with ldd, minus what any desktop provides), the OpenSceneGraph and Qt plugins, start scripts and a README
- ...-light.zip: the same without the libraries; its README lists the packages to install (Fedora: with the Copr and RPM Fusion
  they come from)

The script (multiplayer/package-client.py) lives in the repo, not in a build folder, and can be run by hand: it finds the source
folder from the build's CMakeCache, packages whatever was built, and says clearly what is missing. Linux only for now; the
programs need a C library as new as the builder's, which the README in the zips says.


---
